Your route is never registered because the decorator's @ is missing. Every example in these sections declares a path operation as a decorator, for example:

    @app.get("/items/")
    async def read_items():
        return [{"name": "Foo"}]

Your code has app.get("/") on its own line above async def root(). That is a plain function call whose result is discarded, and root is never attached to the app. With no path operations registered, GET / returns {"detail":"Not Found"} and /docs shows an empty schema, which is exactly what you see. Add the @:

    @app.get("/")
    async def root():
        return {"message": "Hello World"}

This is unrelated to CORS, to uvicorn versus the fastapi CLI, and to your Python version. Note that the docs URLs themselves are configurable (docs_url, redoc_url, openapi_url), and setting openapi_url=None disables the docs UIs, but you have not passed any of those, so the defaults /docs, /redoc, and /openapi.json apply.

